  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed fence at the site constitutes permitted development under Schedule 2, Part 2, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), for the following reasons:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposal consists of the fence and is therefore development of the type described in Class A.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The fence would be 0.85m metres high and would be [adjacent / not adjacent] to a highway used by vehicular traffic. It would therefore not exceed the height limit in paragraph A.1(a) [1 metre adjacent to such a highway / 2 metres elsewhere. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The site is not a listed building, and the fence / wall / gate would not be within the curtilage of a listed building, or surround a listed building. The restriction in paragraph A.1(e) therefore does not apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Permitted development rights for Class A have not been removed by a condition on any planning permission for the site or by an Article 4 direction, and the proposal is not otherwise excluded by article 3 of the Order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the basis of the information submitted, the proposal is lawful and does not require planning permission.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
